In article <1992Feb11.181301.28052@ichips.intel.com> pmeyer@ichips.intel.com (Paul Meyer) writes:
>	How does one identify the alignment of an altar?  I don't see
>anything in the FAQ or the WCST about it.  Several times I've #offered
>at an altar, and it says something implying that two gods (your's and
>the altars) are in conflict or something.  

When the gods are in conflict, you are (in the game's mind) trying to change
the altar to your alignment.  This is done by sacrificing a corpse of a
differently aligned altar when your god is happy with you.

>	Also, how does one change alignment (short of a helm of
>opposite alignment)?  
>	I'm not that impressed with the WCST spoiler file.  It refers
>many times to things you can do after changing alignment, and good
>things to do with co-aligned and non-coaligned altars and priests, but
>doesn't mention how to identify altar alignment or change your
>alignment.  Cover the basics!  (To be fair, it's a big file and I
>could have missed it.  I searched for 'altar' and 'align' and didn't
>see anything.)  help.

Ow, I could be cruel here, but I have learned in the past that people do not
always have the updated versions of the spoilers.  Paul has them up to v.7.00.
Somewhere about 8% of the way into the document under the sections 'General
Hints' is the statement that 'A guaranteed way to change your alignment is to
kill a unicorn of your alignment and offer the fresh corpse at an altar of the
god whose alignment you wish to convert to.'
To tell the alignment of an altar is the same as you would look at any space
you are standing on.  Use the ':' key.  This can always be used to tell you
what the space you are standing on contains...(It is, I believe, in the
help screen of the game).
Also, in the section alignment, it tells you how you can lower your
alignment.  If you get it low enough (like, by sacrificing a friendly unicorn
at the wrong altar) you will change alignment to the altar you are sacrificing
on.  One of the best ways to do this is to kill your pet (at least at the
start of the game, later on your alignment will be too high for such an action
to lower enough to change alignments...)

